I suppose you've entered what's called Bigroom; a large area filled with
monsters that aim towards you, throwing and zapping from distance and may
surround you (which is a bad thing) to hit you in melee from the eight
adjacent places.

> I really have no idea what I'm supposed to do here, I ran back
> upstairs as fast as I could and that's where I am at the moment.

It's just another level, but because of the topology somewhat dangerous.
Somewhere on that level you'll find the downstairs to proceed to a regular
(well known) level topology.

You may engrave the magic word on the stairs to prevent (most) monsters
hitting you. But you are still target from monsters throwing (poisonous)
projectiles or zapping wands at you. So Bigroom handling requires some
preparation; you should be poison resistance and and have enough HP's to
survive some attacks. Don't hesitate to climb up the stairs to heal if
you're getting low on HP's. Having good AC is also very helpful. If you
have only a non-permanent means to engrave the E-word you should have some
offensive wands to zap the monsters from your (quasi) safe spot on the
stairs. A weapon that does much damage (preferable an artifact) also helps.
Fight the monsters that are close, don't wait until you become surrounded.

You may as well circumvent that level, e.g. by digging down if you cannot
reach the staircase (or cannot reach it quickly enough). But keep in mind
that you may want to come back at some time.

You should also be aware that the level below the Oracle also has a second
staicase up that leads to Sokoban. If you want to get the Sokoban price you
may not want to circumvent the level but rather try to reach the second
up-stairs. (All mentioned caveats still apply, though, if passing Bigroom.)

